From 6c31e5e2899606e84a66326957ff2e73ec13a314 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Chong <achong@meta.com>
Date: Mon, 4 Aug 2025 09:39:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] do not throw error if version script is passed to
 darwin

Summary:
# Motivation:
One of the rust libraries used by cuttlefish host utils uses the version script argument in the .bp file. This causes the build to fail.

# Overview:
- remove throwing an error if version script is included on darwin

Normally build/soong should not be modified like this, but this change is exclusively for the darwin host utils branch.

Test Plan:
```
. build/envsetup.sh
 lunch aosp_cf_arm64_phone-userdebug
 m out/host/darwin-x86/cvd-host_package.tar.gz -k &> ~/build.logs.txt
```

Rollback Plan:

Reviewers: tcare, #cuttlefish-cross-platform, benthomas

Reviewed By: tcare

Subscribers: ilyatsunaev, jmgao, ryanyu, <internal-group>

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.intern.facebook.com/D79567136

Tags: aarch64
---
 cc/linker.go | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cc/linker.go b/cc/linker.go
index 3d807a2db..fe3dbc800 100644
--- a/cc/linker.go
+++ b/cc/linker.go
@@ -592,7 +592,7 @@ func (linker *baseLinker) linkerFlags(ctx ModuleContext, flags Flags) Flags {
 
 		if versionScript.Valid() {
 			if ctx.Darwin() {
-				ctx.AddMissingDependencies([]string{"version_script_not_supported_on_darwin"})
+				// ctx.AddMissingDependencies([]string{"version_script_not_supported_on_darwin"})
 			} else {
 				flags.Local.LdFlags = append(flags.Local.LdFlags,
 					config.VersionScriptFlagPrefix+versionScript.String())
